Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:23:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Wake on LAN is sent on the device's own network

- The magic packet went out on the main network only, so a device on a guest or VLAN network was
  listed but never woke. httpd now uses the bridge where the device was last seen (the neighbour
  table, when exactly one bridge has it), else the network whose lease file holds it, else the
  main network; the page says which.
- web.c also carries, for the VPN pages of this rung, each OpenVPN client's mode and effective
  Killswitch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
